    "title": "Backstage Update - Any Injuries Coming Out Of AEW Blood & Guts? - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Clark ,\n10 minutes ago\nAEW’s 2025 Blood & Guts edition of Dynamite is officially in the books, and as you’d expect, several wrestlers are nursing bumps, bruises, and a few battle scars.\nAccording to a report from Fightful Select, Jamie Hayter “got a little banged up” during the Women’s Blood & Guts opener and may have chipped a few teeth. Hayter was “as bad ass as you’d expect,” given how physical the match turned out to be.\nSkye Blue, who bled heavily during the contest, was reportedly okay afterward despite the significant blood loss.\nREAD MORE: Backstage Update – MJF’s AEW Status\nREAD MORE: Injury Update On Buddy Matthews\nAs for Hangman Page and Powerhouse Hobbs, no serious injuries were reported following their brawl that spilled throughout the arena. Both men were said to be sore but in good spirits, with everything going largely as planned.\nFewer wrestlers than usual were brought in for this week’s broadcast, as Dynamite featured only three matches and AEW Collision will air live this weekend rather than being taped immediately after Dynamite.\nAs of this writing, there’s no update yet on the injury status of those involved in the Men’s Blood & Guts main event.\nNOTE: If you have any news tips or podcast recaps that you’d like to send in for us to post (full credit will be given to you), please email me at RClarkPWS@Yahoo.com .",
